WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.138
Cookies and web storage are central to modern browser behavior.

2
00:00:04.138 --> 00:00:12.261
Cookies may maintain state, preferences, tracking context, or authentication-related information for web applications.

3
00:00:12.261 --> 00:00:19.234
Session cookies may be designed to last for a browsing session, while persistent cookies may remain longer.

4
00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:27.816
Their presence can help explain interaction with a site, but they should not be treated as standalone proof of a specific user action.

5
00:00:27.816 --> 00:00:34.023
LocalStorage and sessionStorage are browser-managed storage areas used by web applications.

6
00:00:34.023 --> 00:00:40.460
LocalStorage may persist across sessions, while sessionStorage is generally scoped to a session.

7
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.517
IndexedDB, at a high level, can store larger structured web application data.

8
00:00:45.517 --> 00:00:56.399
Service workers can support offline behavior, background sync, push notifications, and cached application resources depending on site design and browser behavior.

9
00:00:56.399 --> 00:00:59.081
These artifacts can be highly sensitive.

10
00:00:59.081 --> 00:01:07.663
They may contain identifiers, application state, preferences, personal data, account context, or session-related information.

11
00:01:07.663 --> 00:01:15.249
Investigators should avoid credential extraction or misuse and should report only what is relevant and authorized.

12
00:01:15.249 --> 00:01:21.073
The existence of sensitive browser storage calls for privacy discipline, not curiosity.

13
00:01:21.073 --> 00:01:24.675
Authentication state is especially easy to overstate.

14
00:01:24.675 --> 00:01:36.782
A cookie or storage item may show that a browser had state associated with a web application, but it may not prove that a person actively logged in during the precise time window under review.

15
00:01:36.782 --> 00:01:44.138
State can persist, expire, sync, be refreshed automatically, or be created by background application behavior.

16
00:01:44.138 --> 00:01:47.587
The best use of cookies and web storage is contextual.

17
00:01:47.587 --> 00:01:56.859
They can support timelines, show that a browser profile interacted with a service, identify application state, or corroborate other records.

18
00:01:56.859 --> 00:02:04.981
They are strongest when combined with history, downloads, server logs, endpoint telemetry, account logs, and user context.
